  "lineage": "Kalon'ny fahiny ('songs of the past') is a song genre of the Merina highlands that derives from Malagasy-language theatre and operetta. It flourished in 1920–1940 at the Théâtre d'Isotry in Antananarivo, where pieces were written for piano with solo, duet or choral singing in Malagasy, and the pianist-composer Andrianary Ratianarivo founded Troupe Jeannette, which still performs there.",
